+---
+type: decision
+status: active
+updated: 2026-11-03
+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, 3556e27, 0be020e, 4d9b627, 53fe132, c35e1a8, 075e330]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh (incl. tests/gate-denied.list)
+---
+# 0012: Shrink the conductor gate, keep it
+
+**Context.** The "4b" item asked to replace the gate with permission rules plus a ≤50-line gate (`.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md` §1). Replaying 881 conductor Bash calls from 2026-10-18..28 through the gate gave 754 allowed (§3). What was never used: `git show --stat`; `herdr status`, `pane list|layout`, `workspace|tab list`; `gh issue|run|repo|auth|browse`, `pr status`; jq as a pipe consumer (0 allowed). No pipe was ever allowed and `2>&1` was never relied on; 44 of 754 used an unquoted `;` or `&`, which the one-command rule denies and parallel calls replace. No filesystem MCP server is configured. The B′ spike (native subagents instead of the runner) was rejected on 2026-11-03 (`.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`): subagents die on conductor exit ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped"), so the headless runner stays and so does the gate.
+
+**Decision.** Trim to observed usage, keep the gate (552 → 513 lines).
+- Removed: the jq allowlist, `git show`, `git_branch_ok` (now one regex: `git branch` plus any of `-a -r -v --show-current`), herdr beyond `pane get|current`, every gh group except `pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge`, the chain/pipe splitter (replaced by the single-command scanner, 4d9b627), the Agent/Workflow/Monitor/NotebookEdit and `mcp__filesystem__*` cases (the conductor frontmatter `disallowedTools` carries them) and their matcher entries (`Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`). Commits 3556e27, 0be020e. `--via` (a no-op since step 4) is gone from `ask_parse_args` (53fe132).
+- Kept: the path helpers (`rel`, `physrel`, `physical`, raw-stream block): they stop `Read bin/harness`, `..` and symlinks docs→src, which no tool-level deny can express. The Bash allowlist stays: it is what makes "one allowed command" checkable. `tests/gate-denied.list` pins 35 deny probes and the controls.
+- Policy tables (messages, `BASH_ALLOW`, `GH_ALLOW`, `GIT_DENY*`) sit in one labelled block at the top of the gate (c35e1a8).
+- Rejected, option f: express this as `permissions` rules. User-scope rules bind workers too, so the implementer and analyst would lose the tools the gate lets them keep.
+
+**Status.** Active. Closes step 5 of [0011](0011-single-runner-headless.md); supersedes the 4b consequence in [0005](0005-gate-only-inside-herdr.md).
+
+**Consequences.** The gate is still ~500 lines, not 50: the cost of path and quote safety stays. A new conductor command needs a gate line, a `tests/gate.test.sh` case and a "You may run directly" edit in `claude/agents/conductor.md` together. Edit the gate only via a new inode after `bash -n` and the suite ([live gate edit](../troubleshooting/live-gate-edit.md)).
